WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.888
Cao Cao personally led his great army south, pursuing Liu Bei closely, while the people fled in panic, supporting the old and carrying the young.

00:00:10.238 --> 00:00:19.910
At Changban Slope the column fell into chaos, and Liu Bei suddenly discovered that his son A Dou, who had been in his arms, was gone.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:28.780
General Zhao Yun, in silver-white armor on a white steed, turned back alone and charged into the Cao army's formation.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:38.178
Amid thousands of troops he fought bravely, charging left and breaking through right, until at last he found little A Dou beside an earthen wall.

00:00:38.528 --> 00:00:46.184
Zhao Yun held A Dou tightly in his arms, fought his way out through the encirclement, and galloped away.

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:55.318
He safely placed A Dou into Liu Bei's hands, as the morning sun rose and shone on the faces of these friends bound by life and death.

00:00:55.668 --> 00:01:00.180
Liu Bei held the child tightly, so moved that he could not speak.

